{title: Beyond Damascus}
{subtitle: Amos 5:26; 5:27; 5:21–27; Acts 7:42–43}
{key: G}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G] | [G] | [D] | [Em] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I hate I despise your fes[D]tivals
Your so[Em]lemn assemblies bring no delight
Your burnt [C]offerings I [G]will not accept
Your grain offerings give me no plea[Em]sure
Take away from me the [C]noise of your songs
[G]I will not listen to the mu[D]sic of your harps
[Em]But let justice roll on like wa[C]ter
And righteous[G]ness like an ev-er-flow-[D]ing stream
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You [Em]carried Sikkuth your king
And Kiyy[C]un your i[G]mages of the star
The star of [D]your god you made for yourselves
And I [Em]will send you into exile beyond Dam[C]ascus
Says the [G]LORD whose name is the God [D]of hosts
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Did [Em]you bring me [D]sacrifices and of[C]ferings
Those for[G]ty years in the wilderness [D]house of Israel
You car[Em]ried Sikkuth your king again
And Kiyy[C]un your ima[G]ges you made to worship
[D]You turned away to the host of heaven
Car[Em]rying the tent of Molech in your [C]hands
The star of [G]the god Rephan you fol[D]lowed
Your [Em]idols of wood and stone you [C]served
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You [G]carried Sikkuth your king
And Ki[D]yy[G]un your images of the star
[D]The star of your god you made for your[Em]selves
And I will send you into exile [C]beyond Damascus
[G]Says the LORD whose name is the [D]God of hosts
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
So I will [Em]send you in[D]to exile be[C]yond Babylon
[G]Because you worshiped what your [D]hands made
Your festivals [Em]are noise in my [C]ear
Your [G]songs are silence to my [D]heart
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You [Em]carried Sikkuth your king
[C]And Kiyyun [G]your images of the star
The [D]star of your god you made for yourselves
[Em]And I will send you into exile be[C]yond Damascus
[G]Says the LORD whose name is the [D]God of [Em]hosts
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Justice [D]rolls like water [C]now
[G]Righteousness flows like a [D]stream
{end_of_verse}

